% ============================================================
% Task 2: Inductive Generalisation
% Tests whether NARS can form a general rule from two positive
% instances under resource pressure.
%
% Inference mode: Induction (NAL-2)
% Ground truth: <bird --> canFly> with moderate f and c
% ============================================================

% Instance 1: Robin is a bird and robin can fly
<robin --> bird>. %{1.00 0.90}
<robin --> canFly>. %{1.00 0.90}

% Instance 2: Eagle is a bird and eagle can fly
<eagle --> bird>. %{1.00 0.90}
<eagle --> canFly>. %{1.00 0.90}

% Query: Is there a general rule that birds can fly?
<bird --> canFly>?

% Expected: NARS should induce <bird --> canFly> via:
%   robin-->bird + robin-->canFly => bird-->canFly (induction)
%   eagle-->bird + eagle-->canFly => bird-->canFly (induction + revision)
% Ground-truth: f* ~ 0.80, c* ~ 0.45 (weaker than deduction)
